nhanced.webp","description":"Published 2014 enhanced-color Cassini composite, photometrically corrected by Paul Schenk, with nominal 400 m source pixels. Colors extend into ultraviolet and infrared. The dark leading hemisphere is real surface albedo, not a shadow or missing imagery. All supplied pixels are preserved; coarse patches and residual photographed shading remain. Shared Shadows and globe lighting remain active; shape is approximated by a sphere.","summary":"Colors extend into infrared and ultraviolet. The dark leading hemisphere is real surface material, not missing imagery.","title":"Enhanced-color composite"},{"id":"infrared","label":"Infrared","detail":"Partial VIMS","thumbnailUrl":"/scenes/iapetus/iapetus-lens-infrared.webp","description":"Three Cassini VIMS observations from 10 September 2007. False color assigns red to about 2.02 µm, green to 1.59 µm and blue to 1.28 µm. All three channels share a 0–0.45 I/F display range and gamma 2.2; this stretch changes the display only. No photometric correction is applied, so illumination remains. Archive noise filtering and local replacement are retained; original detector defects and potentially affected neighbors are excluded. Gray grid marks unsupported areas and scan gaps.","summary":"Cassini false color: red 2.02, green 1.59, blue 1.28 µm. Coverage is partial; gray grid marks gaps. Illumination and archive filtering remain in these uncorrected measurements.","title":"Cassini VIMS flyby spectra · 10 September 2007"},{"id":"ice-absorption","label":"Ice absorption","detail":"Partial VIMS","thumbnailUrl":"/scenes/iapetus/iapetus-lens-ice-absorption.webp","description":"Near-2.02 µm water-ice band depth relative to a linear 1.82–2.20 µm continuum, using three Cassini VIMS observations from 10 September 2007. This measures absorption strength, not ice abundance. Viewing angle, grain size and noise also affect the values; no photometric correction is applied. Archive noise filtering and local replacement remain; original detector defects and potentially affected neighbors are excluded. Display colors saturate outside 0–0.8; original numerical values are retained. Gray grid marks unsupported areas and scan gaps.","summary":"Near-2.02 µm water-ice absorption in partial Cassini coverage. Gray grid marks gaps. Viewing angle, grain size, noise and archive filtering affect these uncorrected values; they do not measure ice abundance.","legend":{"kind":"scale","title":"Ice absorption","colors":["rgb(49 43 102)","rgb(49 47 105)","rgb(49 51 109)","rgb(49 55 112)","rgb(49 58 116)","rgb(49 62 119)","rgb(49 66 123)","rgb(49 70 126)","rgb(49 74 130)","rgb(49 78 133)","rgb(49 82 137)","rgb(50 85 140)","rgb(50 89 144)","rgb(50 93 147)","rgb(50 97 151)","rgb(50 101 154)","rgb(50 105 158)","rgb(50 109 161)","rgb(50 112 165)","rgb(50 116 168)","rgb(50 120 172)","rgb(50 124 175)","rgb(54 128 176)","rgb(57 132 176)","rgb(61 136 177)","rgb(65 139 177)","rgb(68 143 178)","rgb(72 147 178)","rgb(76 151 179)","rgb(79 155 180)","rgb(83 159 180)","rgb(87 163 181)","rgb(90 166 181)","rgb(94 170 182)","rgb(98 174 182)","rgb(101 178 183)","rgb(105 182 184)","rgb(109 186 184)","rgb(112 190 185)","rgb(116 193 185)","rgb(120 197 186)","rgb(123 201 186)","rgb(127 205 187)","rgb(132 207 187)","rgb(137 209 186)","rgb(143 211 186)","rgb(148 213 185)","rgb(153 215 185)","rgb(158 217 184)","rgb(164 219 184)","rgb(169 221 183)","rgb(174 223 183)","rgb(179 225 182)","rgb(185 228 182)","rgb(190 230 181)","rgb(195 232 181)","rgb(200 234 180)","rgb(206 236 180)","rgb(211 238 179)","rgb(216 240 179)","rgb(221 242 178)","rgb(227 244 178)","rgb(232 246 177)","rgb(237 248 177)"],"labels":["0","0.4","0.8"],"meta":"band-depth fraction","sourceUrl":"https://vims.univ-nantes.fr/cube/1568157352_4"},"title":"Cassini VIMS flyby water-ice absorption · 10 September 2007"}]},"settings":{"title":{"label":"Settings","src":"/shell/title-settings.svg","width":65.55,"height":23,"source":"Inter Variable 4.001 git-9221beed3","sourceUrl":